{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/53878-swift-resolution-and-extended-actions","id":53878,"title":"Swift Resolution and Extended Actions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-20T03:49:57-08:00","id":53878,"title":"Swift Resolution and Extended Actions","content":"If you use Swift Resolution on an Extended Action, does the target still require the normal number of successes? If they do, doesn't that make the power rather useless; same number of successes, far fewer dice.<br /> <br /> If they don't, and only require success on one dice roll doesn't that make the power rather powerful; one success required, just don't fail!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/299-ninedaysdead","name":"NineDaysDead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T17:40:26-08:00","id":54350,"title":"","content":"As far as I can tell, the rules say make a single roll and if the roll succeeds, the action succeeds (no dramatic failure, no exceptional success). I would offer that translating any extended action into a single roll should involve a holistic look at what possible penalties could be involved (what sort of problems would normally be faced on the extended roll). Still, taking this power and the -2 Cover roll that goes with it should not mean that you get ripped off for using it properly.<br /> <br /> I see it as condensing the extended action and all that goes with it to one roll; the advantage is supposed to be the time reduction.<br /> <br /> But yeah, very powerful. Especially if you and a buddy set up a &quot;rai